pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes.iter().filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag)).collect()
}
```
Exact-match against each entry in `tags` (via `any`), preserving input order.

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — the `list` command now parses `--tag <TAG>` from its args, then filters through `filter_by_tag`. No `--tag` → all notes (unchanged behavior). Missing value → prints an error and exits 1.

